==Trivia==
*The word "''Skeleton''" comes from the Greek "''σκελετός''" (''skeletós''), meaning dried up or withered.
**The Skeletons, [[Bomber]], and [[Tombstone]] are the only cards associated with Skeletons that are unlocked in [[Arenas|Bone Pit]].
*The Skeletons are 1 of 19 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Goblins]], [[Barbarians]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Phoenix]], [[Lava Hound]], and the [[Archer Queen]].
**It is the only troop that is only available as a sub-troop in Clash of Clans.
*The Skeletons are 1 of 3 troops which can be spawned by a troop (Skeletons/[[Skeleton Army]]), a [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] ([[Graveyard]]), and a [[:Category:Building Cards|building]] (Tombstone). The others are Goblins and Barbarians.
**Skeletons spawn from more [[cards]] than any other troop, being able to spawn from a total of 8 cards.
*The Skeletons, along with [[Electro Spirit]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Ice Spirit]], [[Warmth]], [[Heal Spirit]], and [[Heal]], are the cheapest cards, costing 1 [[Elixir]].
**The Skeletons were the first [[:Category:1-Elixir Cards|1-Elixir]] card to be added in the game.
*The Skeletons are tied with [[Bats]] and [[Suspicious Bush]] for the lowest hitpoints of all troops, with 119 hitpoints at Level 15, and 32 hitpoints at Level 1. [[Guards]] also have the same hitpoints, however, they come with a shield.
*The Skeletons are one of the first troop cards to be featured in a [[Training Camp|Trainer]]'s [[Battle Decks|deck]], alongside the Minions, Archers, [[Knight]], [[Spear Goblins]], Goblins, Bomber, Barbarians, [[Minion Horde]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, Hog Rider, [[Baby Dragon]], Skeleton Army, Witch, P.E.K.K.A, [[Prince]], and Balloon.
*The Skeletons are one of the first troops to be featured in a [[Loading Screens|Loading Screen]], alongside the Knight, Goblins, and Prince.
*The Skeletons are one of the first troop cards to receive a card render, alongside the Archers, Knight, Goblins, Bomber, Barbarians, Bats, [[Royal Recruits]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Rascals]], Musketeer, Giant, Valkyrie, Wizard, [[Flying Machine]], Hog Rider, [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Zappies]], [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, Skeleton Army, Witch, P.E.K.K.A, Prince, Balloon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, Cannon Cart, [[Mega Knight]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], Lava Hound, [[Night Witch]], and [[Fisherman]].
*The Skeletons are one of the first troop cards to receive a [[Card Evolution]], alongside the Barbarians, [[Royal Giant]], and [[Firecracker]].
*The Skeletons are 1 of 9 troops that have the same sprite for both players, the others are Electro Spirit, Fire Spirit, Bats, Ice Spirit, Heal Spirit, Elixir Blob, Phoenix, and Lava Pup.
*Even though the card spawns 3 Skeletons, the card render displays only 1 Skeleton.
*The Skeletons are 1 of 4 troops which can defeat themselves in one attack, the others being Bats, Firecracker and Wall Breakers.
*Along with the Skeleton Army and [[Wizard Trio]], the Skeletons are the only swarm card whose members spawn all at the exact same time.
*The Skeletons has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Skeletons are 1 of 23 troops that have been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being [[Skeleton Dragons]], Fire Spirit, Bats, [[Elite Barbarians]], Firecracker, Rascal Girls, Royal Hogs, Heal Spirit, Elixir Golem, Guards, Prince, Balloon, Golem, Wall Breakers, Ram Rider, [[Sparky]], Phoenix, Royal Ghost, Bandit, [[Lumberjack]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Monk]].
**The Skeletons have been featured with multiple [[Buff|buffs]]. More specifically:
***The Skeletons are 1 of 3 troops that have been featured with an [[Buff#Invisibility|Invisibility]] buff, the others being Goblins and Bats.
***The Skeletons are the only troop that has been featured with a [[Buff#Shield Boost|Shield Boost]] buff.
*The Skeletons, along with the Minions, Bomber, Skeleton Dragons, Ice Spirit, Mini P.E.K.K.A, [[Mega Minion]], Dart Goblin, [[Ice Golem]], Elixir Golem, [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], Guards, Baby Dragon, P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, Bowler, [[Executioner]], Mega Knight, [[Inferno Dragon]], Royal Ghost, and Lava Hound, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
**An [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Ice_Skeleton ice variant] and a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Lava_Skeleton lava variant] for the Skeleton are also featured as a monster in Squad Buster.
**Also along with the Bats and Royal Recruits, it is also featured as a sub-character in Squad Busters.
*The Skeletons, along with the Archers, Goblins, Barbarians, Mini P.E.K.K.A, Musketeer, Wizard, Witch, Prince, and [[Princess]], are featured as a sticker in [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IMessage iMessage], in a sticker pack called [https://apps.apple.com/us/app/clash-a-rama/id1182384664 Clash-A-Rama].
*According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=BRING-YOUR-CHILD-TO-WORK-DAY_Final.jpg strip], a Skeleton is the Giant Skeleton's child.
*In Royal Crypt, Skeletons can be seen sitting in the audience.
*Using the Skeletons card to summon 15 Skeletons would cost 5 Elixir, whereas using the Skeleton Army card to summon 15 Skeletons costs 3 Elixir.
*The first Trainer the player battles in the Training Camp uses 2 cards, one of them being Skeletons, and the other being Goblins.
*The Skeletons are the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Skeletons are the subject of a few [[Clans|Clan]] badges.
**The Skeletons are the subject of a few [[Emotes]].
***The Skeleton Mariachi Emote may possibly be a reference to [https://brawlstars.fandom.com/wiki/Poco Poco] from Brawl Stars, another Supercell game.
**The Skeletons are the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Red vs Blue frame is created by Myoho.
***In the [https://youtu.be/Q5e94mUB7Mc?si=GCn1Mhk7dIPe4ih2 Raise your Battle Banners trailer], there was a Battle Banner decoration that showed a Skeleton riding a tusk like a snowboard. However, this Battle Banner decoration never made it to the game.
*In the Thai language setting of the game, the card description incorrectly states that the card spawns 4 Skeletons. This is likely due to the fact that the card used to spawn 4 Skeletons.
*The Skeletons were featured in the winning deck of the [https://youtu.be/LWQjS0e6iiE Super Magical Cup Tournament], by a player called CMcHugh.
*Before the Skeletons' card release, the Skeletons' hitpoints and damage were increased by 8%.

